/* 【2026-08-09 / FEAT-489 Phase 5 (v1.1 G4)】iOS native permission dialogs, English.

   These are NOT covered by the Flutter ARB —— they are rendered by iOS itself,
   so the only way to localize them is this file. Declaring `en` in
   CFBundleLocalizations without this file would show the Japanese strings
   (with the 🪶 marker) to English speakers inside a system dialog.

   Tone follows the English Sabi voice established in FEAT-489 Phase 2F-b
   (gentle, unhurried, 🪶 as the closing marker —— 322 of the 1,488 English
   ARB strings carry it). Keep it consistent with `app_en.arb`.

   ⚠️ When changing wording, update `ja.lproj/InfoPlist.strings` and the
   fallback values in `Info.plist` as well.
*/

/* Free memo voice input (FEAT-499). Sabi voice + 🪶 marker */
"NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription" = "Speech recognition lets you set down a passing thought in your own voice. 🪶";
"NSMicrophoneUsageDescription" = "The microphone is used to receive what you say. 🪶";

/* Inquiry screenshot attachment (FEAT-366).
   Deliberately plain rather than in Sabi's voice —— Apple's guideline asks for a
   concrete statement of need, and a direct explanation reads better here
   (mirrors the original intent recorded in Info.plist). */
"NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription" = "Access to your photo library is needed so you can attach a screenshot to an inquiry.";
